{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-06-06T21:20:53.694Z","evidence":{"seeds":"trellis-4ba0","commit":"10738c1765116a7d6cb1fe81712cec2187e7c255"},"title":"Investigation core: 4 areas + per-area zod findings + pure deterministic grader","rationale":"trellis-4ba0 builds src/investigation/ as the agent→facts→grade seam (SPEC §7). areas.ts: AREA_IDS/AREAS keyed by the rubric 'investigation' values (documentation/agent-config/setup-runnability/test-layout); each Area carries id/title/description/facts[]+a prompt rendered by a shared buildPrompt scaffold (read-only mandate, facts-not-verdicts, submit_findings EXACTLY ONCE) so the only per-area variable is the fact list. findings.ts: one z.strictObject per area (strict ALL the way down) so verdict-shaped extras are rejected at the boundary; the §7.2 AgentConfigFindings example is the shape model, finalized for all four; test-layout adds a superRefine (matchingConvention<=fileCount) fact-sanity invariant; FINDINGS_SCHEMAS+AreaFindings map area id→schema/type. grader.ts: pure, no I/O/clock/random. Grade shape mirrors DetectorResult/ScorecardEntry (denominator literal 1, naKind iff numerator null) so agent grades fold into the scorecard on the same path. Per-area typed grader maps (satisfies Record<string,(f)=>Grade>); CRITERION_AREA derived from those maps; gradeArea(area,raw) parses then grades all bound criteria, gradeCriterion(id,raw) grades one. §3.2 enforced structurally: SKIPPABLE_AGENT_CRITERIA={local_services_setup,devcontainer_runnable,flaky_test_detection}; enforceSkippable() throws if a non-skippable criterion grades N/A. Skippable graders emit not-applicable (surface absent) vs no-detector (ambiguous, e.g. devcontainer present but buildability unknown). FRESH_THRESHOLD_DAYS=180 for documentation_freshness. Tests: table-driven (facts→outcome) covering pass/fail/N-A for all 20; determinism (same facts→toEqual); acceptance loads the REAL rubric and asserts gradedCriterionIds()===20 agent ids, CRITERION_AREA matches each criterion.investigation, skippable flags agree.","id":"mx-76d926","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-09-19T16:06:59.953Z","archive_reason":"manual: Superseded by the current deterministic audit architecture and source cleanup; see SPEC.md and AGENTS.md."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-06-06T21:40:18.280Z","evidence":{"commit":"5a88deb119e76d67e8a4dc1dfef94b7365368056"},"relates_to":["mx-76d926"],"title":"Pi RPC provider: single investigate() entrypoint, injectable spawn, no-fabricated-pass degradation","rationale":"trellis-98b5 builds src/investigation/provider/ as the one Pi transport (SPEC §9): pi/argv.ts (locked read-only argv + §9.4 provider/model precedence), pi/env.ts (env-passthrough only, never argv; PI_PROVIDER_ENV_KEYS map), pi/findings-extension.ts (registers submit_findings; parameter JSON-schema via zod v4 native z.toJSONSchema, NOT the zod-to-json-schema package — zod is v4 so it's built in; the extension uses minimal structural pi types since @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent is not a trellis dep), pi/session.ts (the §9.3 state machine: hold stdin open, capture submit_findings toolCall off the assistant message_end event stream, zod-validate, corrective retries, heartbeat watchdog), pi/version.ts (minimum-version probe → degrade not crash). The process boundary is an injectable PiSpawn so the whole loop is tested against a scripted fake pi (fake-pi.ts) with zero network. Every failure path resolves no-detector with a rationale, never a fabricated pass. Anthropic anthropic-provider serialization reads schema.properties/.required, so a plain JSON-schema works as pi tool parameters without a TypeBox runtime.","id":"mx-92801c","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-09-19T16:06:59.953Z","archive_reason":"manual: Superseded by the current deterministic audit architecture and source cleanup; see SPEC.md and AGENTS.md."}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-06-06T21:51:18.637Z","evidence":{"seeds":"trellis-f478","commit":"3911df8226fd2fd747d64e5aace8868f9ca2ee32"},"relates_to":["mx-92801c"],"name":"Investigation golden harness: replay frozen pi RPC streams offline → grader","description":"trellis-f478 adds src/investigation/golden.ts + __golden__/<area>.jsonl (one canonicalized pi --mode rpc stream per area + corrupted.jsonl) + golden.test.ts. Design: (1) canonicalizePiStream walks parsed JSONL and collapses volatile fields to fixed placeholders by KEY NAME (id/sessionId/responseId/...→ all-zero uuid; timestamp/createdAt/...→ epoch; usage→{inputTokens:0,outputTokens:0}; cost/*Ms→0) — recursive, idempotent, so the test asserts each frozen file === canonicalizePiStream(file). Generated the frozen bytes via a throwaway script that pipes hand-authored envelope arrays through canonicalizePiStream (NOT hand-typed) to guarantee byte-canonical JSON.stringify key order. (2) Offline replay reuses makeFakePi: a golden = ONE FakeTurn (the recorded envelope array) released on the initial prompt; run through real investigate(repo,area,{spawn:fake.spawn,sourceEnv:{}}) so parser→zod→grader is the real path, no pi/network. Corrupted golden replays the SAME turn 3x (initial+2 correctives) to drive corrective→no-detector; a smuggled verdict key 'passed' is rejected by strictObject (zod code unrecognized_keys). (3) scripts/update-pi-golden.ts is DOUBLE-GATED (TRELLIS_UPDATE_PI_GOLDEN=1 AND --live) — refuses otherwise, returning exit 1 not a crash; capturingSpawn wraps defaultPiSpawn and stdout.tee()s one branch into a chunk buffer while the session reads the other. Gotchas: biome cognitive-complexity max 15 (extracted canonicalizeField helper); __golden__ already excluded from biome/jscpd/check:agents; fixtures hand-authored & marked as such in __golden__/README.md per SPEC §9.7 bootstrap note.","files":[".seeds/issues.jsonl","AGENTS.md","RUNBOOK.md"],"id":"mx-415b88","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-09-19T16:06:59.953Z","archive_reason":"manual: Superseded by the current deterministic audit architecture and source cleanup; see SPEC.md and AGENTS.md."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-06-06T22:06:13.993Z","evidence":{"seeds":"trellis-4222","commit":"acfe78ef60ee9a8f29a497009d515c0915f98633"},"relates_to":["mx-92801c"],"title":"Investigation wired into audit: cache-or-investigate per area, repo-wide grade projected onto app-scope","rationale":"trellis-4222 adds src/investigation/run.ts (runInvestigation): per-area investigation_cache lookup keyed (repo, commit_sha, area) → miss fills via one bounded investigate() → zod-revalidate → cache write; --no-cache skips the lookup but still writes. Pi is probed ONCE and only when a miss exists, so a fully-cached re-run never spawns Pi (a commit stays auditable after Pi is uninstalled); a failed probe or per-area failure degrades to ok:false → no-detector naming the area+reason (never a fabricated pass). build.ts auditRepo gains opts.investigation (absent → agent criteria stay AGENT_NOT_WIRED for backward compat); a repo-scope Grade IS a ScorecardEntry, while app-scope criteria (test-layout) project the single repo-wide verdict uniformly across N apps (pass→N/N, fail→0/N, N/A→null/N) preserving the grader's fact-rich rationale rather than re-synthesizing it. resolveCommit now appends -dirty when git status --porcelain is non-empty so cache keys never lie. CLI: store doubles as run-history + cache (skipped entirely under --no-persist so no DB file is created); TRELLIS_PI_BIN overrides the pi binary (tests set it bogus for hermetic degradation since pi is installed locally).","id":"mx-027f12","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-09-19T16:06:59.953Z","archive_reason":"manual: Superseded by the current deterministic audit architecture and source cleanup; see SPEC.md and AGENTS.md."}
{"type":"failure","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-06-07T00:22:45.702Z","evidence":{"seeds":"trellis-a534","commit":"e5bfa12f5ac9b193a02c4daafeed3ee4b67e967b"},"dir_anchors":["src/report"],"description":"Pi version probe degraded ALL investigation criteria to no-detector in every real audit: defaultVersionSpawn read only stdout (stderr:'ignore'), but pi 0.78.x prints its version to STDERR. probePiVersion got an empty string and reported 'could not parse a version'. Self-audit was stuck at L3 (coverage clamp) purely because investigation never ran — goldens hid it since tests inject a fake spawn returning stdout.","resolution":"VersionSpawn now also captures stderr (stderr:'pipe'); probePiVersion parses the union stdout+stderr. Added a regression test (fakeSpawnStreams) for the stderr-only case. Live probe now returns {ok:true,version:'0.78.1'} and trellis self-audit bands L4 (coverage 78%).","id":"mx-e5afdd","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-09-19T16:06:59.953Z","archive_reason":"manual: Superseded by the current deterministic audit architecture and source cleanup; see SPEC.md and AGENTS.md."}
